    "lawCode": "Rpld & add Art 7 §§110 - 112, State L",
    "lawSection": "State Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8172A\n\nSPONSOR: GIANARIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the state law, in relation to creation of congressional\ndistricts; and to repeal article 7 of such law relating thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to establish 26 Congressional districts.\ndistricts.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would:\n\n-- provide County, County Subdivisions, Census Tract, and Census Block\ndescriptions of 26 Congressional districts.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nThis bill would amend the State law to provide for the reapportionment\nof the New York State Congressional districts.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill establishes new Congressional districts for the State of New\nYork. It is based on population figures from the 2020 Federal Census.\nAs proposed, the Congressional districts comply with the United States\nand New York State Constitutions and the requirements of the Federal\nVoting Rights Act.\n\nThis legislation has been introduced pursuant to the provisions of the\nState Constitution and Chapter 633 of the Laws of 2021.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately, provided that the provisions of\nsection four of this act shall take effect January 1, 2023.\n",
